comment = "Hardware-assisted execution tracing (Intel PT, Intel CPUs only)"

desc = <<EOD
bsdtrace captures every branch a program takes using Intel Processor
Trace via the hwt(4) framework, then decodes the trace into
symbolized control-flow events (calls, returns, jumps, syscalls)
with per-function profiles, call trees, and flame-graph output.
Traces are saved for offline analysis.

Intel Processor Trace is an Intel-only CPU feature: this package
requires an amd64 system with an Intel CPU and does not work on AMD
processors. The underlying hwt(4) framework itself is cross-platform
(ARM SPE is supported on arm64).
EOD
